WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.945
Welcome to our training on how to read Amazon Business Reports.

00:00:02.945 --> 00:00:06.693
Amazon Business Reports can help you monitor your product's sales, traffic, and conversion rates.

00:00:06.693 --> 00:00:10.976
They can also show the effects of changes that you have made in your selling strategy.

00:00:10.976 --> 00:00:13.921
Business reports are found in Seller Central under the Reports tab.

00:00:13.921 --> 00:00:16.866
These reports are available if you have the professional selling plan.

00:00:16.866 --> 00:00:28.912
Let's look at a few examples of  how the data in the business reports can help you understand your

00:00:28.912 --> 00:00:29.180
sales.

00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:33.835
In order to make a sale, customers must visit your product's detail page.

00:00:33.835 --> 00:00:38.491
Sessions and page view metrics show the traffic to your product's detail page.

00:00:38.491 --> 00:00:42.072
The more traffic, the greater the chance of a sale.

00:00:42.072 --> 00:00:47.085
Page view metrics display the total number of visits to your product's detail page.

00:00:47.085 --> 00:00:52.099
A customer may visit the same detail page multiple times a day or week.

00:00:52.099 --> 00:00:55.680
Each of these visits counts as a single page view.

00:00:55.680 --> 00:01:00.756
The sessions metric displays the number of customers that are visiting your page per day.

00:01:00.756 --> 00:01:07.523
A customer may visit the same detail page multiple times in one day, but as this is the same customer,

00:01:07.523 --> 00:01:12.260
all of the customer's visits for that day will only count as one session.

00:01:12.260 --> 00:01:15.748
Maria can't decide which wine glasses to buy.

00:01:15.748 --> 00:01:19.672
She keeps visiting any company's Stemless Glasses detail page.

00:01:19.672 --> 00:01:25.340
Maria visits any company's Stemless Glasses product detail page seven times on Saturday.

00:01:25.340 --> 00:01:29.080
On Tuesday, she visits the page again to buy the glasses.

00:01:29.080 --> 00:01:35.540
The page view value in the reports is eight, as she visits the detail page for the glasses eight

00:01:35.540 --> 00:01:36.560
times in total.

00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:44.366
The sessions value is two, as Maria is the same customer visiting and has visited on two separate

00:01:44.366 --> 00:01:44.800
days.

00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:50.960
Comparing report metrics can help you determine the reasons why sales have increased, decreased,

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:52.280
or leveled off.

00:01:52.280 --> 00:01:59.040
Comparisons can also help you decide if using other Amazon selling tools may help your sales.

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:04.683
Here are a few examples of things you may want to consider when there are changes in business report

00:02:04.683 --> 00:02:04.980
data.

00:02:04.980 --> 00:02:11.680
If your page views are high but your sales are low, ask, is your product priced correctly?

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:14.330
Could your product be better described?

00:02:14.330 --> 00:02:16.980
Could your product images be better?

00:02:16.980 --> 00:02:22.280
Should you consider becoming a prime seller or using fulfillment by Amazon?

00:02:22.280 --> 00:02:24.336
More questions to ask yourself.

00:02:24.336 --> 00:02:29.680
How do the session and page views correlate to your percentage featured offer?

00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:33.180
Do you get more traffic when you are the featured offer?

00:02:33.180 --> 00:02:34.320
Featured offer considerations.

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:41.160
If you have low featured offer percentage and low sales but your product detail page has had high

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:41.920
page views,

00:02:41.920 --> 00:02:47.960
you may want to consider reducing the price of your product to try and become the featured offer.

00:02:47.960 --> 00:02:55.006
Also, consider using the automatic pricing tool so that you can match or beat the featured offer

00:02:55.006 --> 00:02:55.420
price.

00:02:55.420 --> 00:02:56.864
Fulfillment by Amazon considerations.

00:02:56.864 --> 00:03:01.920
If you have a high number of page views and sessions for your product,

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:07.320
you may want to consider that product for fulfillment by Amazon, FBA.

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:11.520
Using FBA can help convert page views to sales.

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:17.962
You can also compare the data in the reports before, during and after an event to determine its

00:03:17.962 --> 00:03:18.320
success.

00:03:18.320 --> 00:03:26.920
Events include Prime Day, being the featured offer, advertising and campaigns, coupons and deals,

00:03:26.920 --> 00:03:32.920
automatic pricing for the product, an increase or decrease in the price of the product.

00:03:32.920 --> 00:03:37.920
Sales trends are useful in seeing how your product is selling over time.

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:44.836
Here are a few examples of questions to ask yourself about the product and why sales increased or

00:03:44.836 --> 00:03:45.220
decreased.

00:03:45.220 --> 00:03:46.856
Is your product seasonal?

00:03:46.856 --> 00:03:49.720
Are you no longer the featured offer?

00:03:49.720 --> 00:03:52.920
Have you changed the price of the product?

00:03:52.920 --> 00:03:58.120
Was the product a temporarily in demand product owing to social media coverage?

00:03:58.120 --> 00:04:01.020
Was your product out of stock?

00:04:01.020 --> 00:04:05.594
The seller performance report shows your performance metrics for customer satisfaction.

00:04:05.594 --> 00:04:08.920
It is important to regularly review this report,

00:04:08.920 --> 00:04:11.920
especially the return and feedback data.

00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:17.520
Reviewing and acting on this data will help ensure that your account remains in good health.

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:24.563
Amazon Business Reports provide a wealth of information that can be downloaded into a CSV file or

00:04:24.563 --> 00:04:26.220
viewed in Seller Central.

00:04:26.220 --> 00:04:30.520
This concludes the training on how to read Amazon Business Reports.

00:04:30.520 --> 00:04:33.680
Thank you, and happy selling in the Amazon Store.
